      "category": "struct",
      "role": "shared-struct",
      "size": 104,
      "alignment": 8,
      "doc": "The volume a view sees, as the planes that bound it in world space (ADR-0057): what the renderer culls against, public so a game culls or streams its own chunks and cells by the same maths. Each plane is a `Vec4` whose xyz is its unit normal pointing into the volume and whose w is its distance, so a point `p` is on the inside of it when `dot(xyz, p) + w >= 0`.",
